<article class="env-lemma" id="05EA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05EA">Lemma <span data-tag="05EA">15.90.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $I$ be an ideal of $R$. For any $R$-module $M$ set $M[I^ n] = \{ m \in M \mid I^ nm = 0\} $. If $I$ is finitely generated then the following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$M[I] = 0$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$M[I^ n] = 0$ for all $n \geq 1$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $I = (f_1, \ldots , f_ t)$, then the map $M \to \bigoplus M_{f_ i}$ is injective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0565" data-tag="0565">10.24.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>